  "prompt": "Use case: illustration-story. Asset type: Japanese elementary vocabulary illustrations, sheet 20. Edit the provided 2048x2048 template, painting ONLY inside its sixteen white panels. Every single panel MUST have identical width and height. All horizontal lines must be EXACTLY at 0%,25%,50%,75%,100%, not based on artwork. Keep precisely the 4x4 equal grid and 5 continuous pure magenta #ff00ff lines in each direction, including outer frame. Preserve line position, width and full canvas. Each panel is an independent clear gentle picture-book illustration as isolated vignettes on a pure white background, large and easily understood. Never use magenta for illustration. Avoid all pink, purple and neon colors in artwork, objects, decorations, lighting and shadows. Use warm orange, red, yellow, green, blue and neutral colors. No pink/purple concert lights. Nothing crosses the grid. No text, letters, numbers, labels, symbols resembling writing or watermarks. For abstract words show a concrete situation illustrating the meaning. Diverse natural children and adults, no stereotypes. Correct anatomy and objects. Panels in strict row-major order (left to right, top to bottom):\n1. 香り — 花や食べ物などから感じるよいにおい。\n2. 価格 — 品物などの値段。\n3. 科学技術 — 科学の知識を使って暮らしなどに役立てる技術。\n4. 科学者 — 自然の仕組みなどを科学で調べる人。\n5. 輝き — きらきらと光っている様子。\n6. 書き方 — 文字や文章を書く方法。\n7. 書き言葉 — 文章に書くときに使う言葉。\n8. 書き込み — 本や掲示板などに文字を書き加えること。\n9. 書き初め — 新しい年に初めて筆で文字を書くこと。\n10. 書き取り — 聞いた言葉などを文字に書くこと。\n11. 垣根 — 敷地の境などに作る囲い。\n12. 覚悟 — 難しいことなどに向き合おうと心を決めること。\n13. 各種 — いろいろな種類。\n14. 各自 — 一人一人それぞれ。\n15. 画数 — 漢字などを形作る点や線の数。\n16. 拡大 — 大きくしたり範囲を広げたりすること。\nSafety and clarity: Vehicles must be driven only by unmistakable adults, never children. Industrial machinery and knives are used by adults. Do not put a child in a car driver's seat. Keep artwork separated by the measured template grid.\n",
